# Include

This directory contains header files used by the ESP32 Air Pen firmware.

Header files can be used to organise function declarations, hardware configurations, constants and shared definitions separately from the main application code.

## Purpose

- Store custom header files.
- Define hardware pin configurations.
- Declare reusable functions and classes.
- Organise shared project settings.

## Structure

```text
include/
└── README.md
```

Custom header files can be added here as the project grows.

Currently, the main firmware implementation is maintained in `src/main.cpp`.